  "worked_solution": "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p=1$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q=-6$, so the distance we move is $|q|=6.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *negative*, we move $6$ units to the *left* from $1.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14152428/assets/f488d1dc3787fefc588e143e7808fee7e4473a9918986b49bc36344e6a153b25.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n1+(-6)=-5.\n$$",
